From 3eca0207370485bb591206605d3c10d38cecd788 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Tue, 20 Oct 2026 15:13:11 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 3/4] Tighten contract derivations: exact balances, one
 currency, sector rules

Fixes the review findings on the contract-derivation batch:
- averages use the exact opening (day before the fiscal year) and closing
  year-end instants; an interim balance never substitutes
- every monetary input must share the numerator's currency and unit
- a missing debt line is not zero; a reported zero still counts
- the tax expense keeps its sign (expense <= 0); benefit, loss and rates
  outside [0, 1) withhold NOPAT, ROIC and incremental ROIC
- banks, insurers and issuers without a known industry are excluded; the
  pipeline passes the company's industry to the calculator
- working-capital turnover needs positive, material balances
- per-share growth keeps one share basis and a positive prior value
- the debt-service proxy keeps principal when interest is zero
- quarter changes need the contiguous previous quarter, same currency
  and a positive base
- fixed_charge_coverage is DEFINITION_PENDING and never emitted

